  "title": "Avoir (to have) — Present Tense",
  "prerequisiteIds": ["fr-lesson-etre"],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "explanation", "markdown": "**Avoir** (to have) is also irregular:\n\nj'**ai** · tu **as** · il/elle **a** · nous **avons** · vous **avez** · ils/elles **ont**\n\nFrench uses *avoir* idiomatically where English uses \"to be\": **avoir faim** (to be hungry), **avoir soif** (to be thirsty), **avoir chaud/froid** (to be hot/cold), and **avoir ... ans** (to be ... years old)." },
    { "type": "exercise", "exerciseId": "fr-ex-avoir-1" },
    { "type": "exercise", "exerciseId": "fr-ex-avoir-2" },
    { "type": "exercise", "exerciseId": "fr-ex-avoir-3" }
  ],
  "exercises": [
